1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,437
One More, Please!

3
00:00:03,437 --> 00:00:06,510
It's Saturday morning, and the bakery smells amazing.

4
00:00:06,510 --> 00:00:07,906
Warm bread.

5
00:00:07,906 --> 00:00:09,437
Sweet cinnamon.

6
00:00:09,437 --> 00:00:11,115
And something buttery.

7
00:00:11,115 --> 00:00:12,906
Dad smiles at me.

8
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:15,463
You're ordering today, Lucy.

9
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:16,806
Me?

10
00:00:17,044 --> 00:00:18,090
Yep.

11
00:00:18,090 --> 00:00:19,767
I'll be right here.

12
00:00:20,044 --> 00:00:21,173
Okay.

13
00:00:21,173 --> 00:00:22,704
I can do this.

14
00:00:22,704 --> 00:00:24,934
The woman behind the counter waves.

15
00:00:25,204 --> 00:00:26,364
Hi there!

16
00:00:26,364 --> 00:00:28,010
What can I get for you?

17
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:30,854
Could I have two cinnamon rolls, please?

18
00:00:31,084 --> 00:00:32,224
Sure!

19
00:00:32,224 --> 00:00:33,869
For here or to go?

20
00:00:34,156 --> 00:00:35,618
I look at Dad.

21
00:00:35,618 --> 00:00:37,931
He points to the little paper bags.

22
00:00:37,931 --> 00:00:39,743
To go, please.

23
00:00:39,743 --> 00:00:41,764
The woman reaches for a bag.

24
00:00:41,764 --> 00:00:44,264
Then I remember my little brother, Ben.

25
00:00:44,264 --> 00:00:47,827
He's at home, probably asking Mom when breakfast is coming.

26
00:00:47,827 --> 00:00:50,098
Actually, could we make that three?

27
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:51,676
Of course.

28
00:00:51,676 --> 00:00:53,415
Three cinnamon rolls.

29
00:00:53,692 --> 00:00:55,611
Dad raises an eyebrow.

30
00:00:55,852 --> 00:00:57,802
Who's the third one for?

31
00:00:58,036 --> 00:00:59,194
Ben!

32
00:00:59,428 --> 00:01:00,807
Good thinking.

33
00:01:00,807 --> 00:01:03,703
He'd notice if we came home smelling like cinnamon.

34
00:01:03,988 --> 00:01:05,305
I laugh.

35
00:01:05,305 --> 00:01:08,555
Then I spot a tray of tiny cookies shaped like cats.

36
00:01:08,555 --> 00:01:10,357
One has a crooked ear.

37
00:01:10,357 --> 00:01:12,805
It looks a little like our cat, Noodle.

38
00:01:12,805 --> 00:01:14,388
Dad, look!

39
00:01:14,388 --> 00:01:15,930
That one's Noodle.

40
00:01:16,204 --> 00:01:17,904
It does look like him.

41
00:01:18,124 --> 00:01:19,982
Can we get a cookie, too?

42
00:01:19,982 --> 00:01:21,764
Dad checks the bag.

43
00:01:22,036 --> 00:01:24,111
Let's stick with the rolls today.

44
00:01:24,340 --> 00:01:25,469
Okay.

45
00:01:25,469 --> 00:01:27,042
Maybe next time.

46
00:01:27,042 --> 00:01:29,198
The woman hands me our breakfast.

47
00:01:29,198 --> 00:01:30,573
How much is it?

48
00:01:30,844 --> 00:01:32,846
Nine dollars, please.

49
00:01:33,076 --> 00:01:35,549
Dad pays, and I take the bag.

50
00:01:35,549 --> 00:01:37,622
It's warm against my fingers.

51
00:01:37,622 --> 00:01:40,007
Could we have a few napkins, please?

52
00:01:40,276 --> 00:01:41,655
Absolutely.

53
00:01:41,655 --> 00:01:43,093
Here you go.

54
00:01:43,372 --> 00:01:44,564
Thank you!

55
00:01:44,564 --> 00:01:46,074
Have a nice day!

56
00:01:46,348 --> 00:01:47,923
You, too!

57
00:01:48,148 --> 00:01:50,431
Outside, Dad grins.

58
00:01:50,668 --> 00:01:52,691
You handled that really well.

59
00:01:52,924 --> 00:01:54,366
I grin back.

60
00:01:54,366 --> 00:01:57,032
I only forgot Ben for about three seconds.

61
00:01:57,032 --> 00:01:59,543
At home, Ben runs to the door.

62
00:01:59,812 --> 00:02:01,439
Did you get me anything?

63
00:02:01,660 --> 00:02:03,300
I hold up the bag.

64
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:05,008
One cinnamon roll.

65
00:02:05,008 --> 00:02:06,362
Just for you.

66
00:02:06,628 --> 00:02:08,130
You're the best!

67
00:02:08,356 --> 00:02:10,777
Noodle walks over and sniffs the bag.

68
00:02:10,777 --> 00:02:12,568
Sorry, Noodle,

69
00:02:12,568 --> 00:02:13,912
I tell him.

70
00:02:13,912 --> 00:02:15,881
Your breakfast is in your bowl.

71
00:02:15,881 --> 00:02:18,256
He flicks his tail and walks away.

72
00:02:18,256 --> 00:02:19,787
Dad laughs.

73
00:02:20,068 --> 00:02:22,539
I think he wants to speak to the manager.
